@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `usca-holidays`

-- Tests of usca-holidays.l4.  Expected values are decided from the section cited, or by a short Python script written from the statute text
-- that uses only Python's own calendar (it is not part of this row), never from the module.  A failing assertion is a finding.

GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`days supplied, March 31 stays` MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 2 17), (YMD 2027 2 6))
        `Diwali days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 11 8))
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 6 5))
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS (LIST (YMD 2025 11 27), (YMD 2026 11 26))
        `Good Friday days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 4 3))
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 3 27))
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS TRUE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 7 3), (YMD 2030 9 2))
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 5 15))
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 8 14))

GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`days supplied, March 31 does not stay` MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 2 17), (YMD 2027 2 6))
        `Diwali days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 11 8))
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 6 5))
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS (LIST (YMD 2025 11 27), (YMD 2026 11 26))
        `Good Friday days` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 4 3))
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 3 27))
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS FALSE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 7 3), (YMD 2030 9 2))
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 5 15))
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS (LIST (YMD 2026 8 14))

GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`days supplied with only section 135 days` MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS EMPTY
        `Diwali days` IS EMPTY
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS EMPTY
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS EMPTY
        `Good Friday days` IS EMPTY
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS EMPTY
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS TRUE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS (LIST YMD 2030 9 2)
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS EMPTY
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`a moment on` d `at second` s MEANS Moment WITH `the day` IS d, `seconds after midnight` IS s


§ `Dates named by the calendar`

-- The n-th given weekday of a month (weekday 0 is Sunday).  Hand check: January 2026 begins on a Thursday, so its Mondays are 5, 12, 19, 26.
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 1 1 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 5)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 1 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 19)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 4 1 1 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 26)
-- Every combination for a handful of months, against Python's calendar.
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 2 2024 EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 19)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 4 5 9 2025 EQUALS (YMD 2025 9 26)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 1 10 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 10 12)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 2 2028 EQUALS (YMD 2028 2 21)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 1 9 2030 EQUALS (YMD 2030 9 2)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 0 3 2027 EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 14)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 0 11 2027 EQUALS (YMD 2027 11 7)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 0 3 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 8)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 0 3 2024 EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 10)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 5 3 5 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 3)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 0 9 2024 EQUALS (YMD 2024 9 1)
#ASSERT `the n-th given weekday of a month` 4 4 11 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 11 26)
-- The last Monday in May: 2024-05-27, 2025-05-26, 2026-05-25, 2027-05-31, 2028-05-29, 2030-05-27.
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2024 EQUALS (YMD 2024 5 27)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2025 EQUALS (YMD 2025 5 26)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 25)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2027 EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 31)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2028 EQUALS (YMD 2028 5 29)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2030 EQUALS (YMD 2030 5 27)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 25)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 2027 EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 31)
-- The last Sunday of February, leap and common.
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 0 2 2024 EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 25)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 0 2 2026 EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 22)
#ASSERT `the last given weekday of a month` 0 2 2028 EQUALS (YMD 2028 2 27)
#ASSERT `the date is the given day of the given month` (YMD 2026 7 4) 7 4
#ASSERT NOT (`the date is the given day of the given month` (YMD 2026 7 5) 7 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`the date is the given day of the given month` (YMD 2026 8 4) 7 4)

§ `Gov. Code § 6700(a): the days the text fixes by the calendar`

-- Paragraphs (2), (5), (6), (8), (10)-(18): January 1, February 12, third Monday in February, April 24, last Monday in May, June 19, July 4,
-- first Monday in September, September 9, fourth Friday in September, second Monday in October, November 11, December 25.
