§ `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), § 6701(c): March 31 and an observed day`

-- § 6701(c): when March 31 falls on a Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday the Legislature may observe it on a Friday or Monday instead.  31 March 2026 is a Tuesday; the caller supplies Friday 27 March as observed.
-- The text does not say whether 31 March itself then stops being a holiday, so the caller says.
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 stays` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 stays` (YMD 2026 3 27)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 does not stay` (YMD 2026 3 31))
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 does not stay` (YMD 2026 3 27)
-- A year with no observed day supplied: March 31 stays whichever way the flag is set.
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 stays` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 does not stay` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `days supplied, March 31 does not stay` (YMD 2025 3 31)
-- Nothing supplied: March 31 is a holiday, the 27th is not.
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `no day is supplied` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `no day is supplied` (YMD 2026 3 27))
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` `no day is supplied` (YMD 2026 3 30))

